{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794770670,"nonce":"wJHPjmDA/xypHPTv63L3J/8xyi4=","message":"Written as ~/Vibranium/hxn-gpu-webgl2, commit 1c158c9, local only: no GitHub repository yet. API is hxn-gpu-gles's on the web page's canvas (Context.create, setSize, width, height in place of Display). Emscripten backend calls Emscripten's GLES 3 directly (link-args -sMIN_WEBGL_VERSION=2 -sMAX_WEBGL_VERSION=2). Ash backend: wire from Khronos webgl.idl and webgl2.idl, xgpu's canvas.idl and an agent.idl of helpers for what WebGL answers as any (compile and link status, getParameter), a sampler uniform lookup, and completed() as a promise over a fence. Non-byte texture uploads go through a pixel unpack buffer, since WebGL takes them only as a typed array of their type.\n\nRun locally on macOS, headless Chrome: hxn check cpp --wasm --browser (3 runs) and hxn check hl --wasm --threads --browser (4 runs, 3 with HXN_PAGE_CORES=3) all pass: render, textured, buffer, canvas, getError 0 at the end. The Ash runs used hxn 4cb0181 (unpushed archive link) and Ash's tree. Not run: Linux with SwiftShader (CI flags --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader are untested), a packaged haxelib.\n\nCI pins hxn cbf7e13 and Ash v0.1.18 like hxn-gpu-webgpu, so it builds the Ash side module and keeps llvm-tools; README and skill already describe the --native-lib link. Both drivers are repinned together after the Ash release.\n\nOpen for hxn-gpu (4db10ab): under Ash, gpu_webgpu.mjs transfers the canvas to its Worker when Instance.create starts the agent, so a program that tries WebGPU and then falls back to WebGL2 finds the canvas taken. The fallback needs the decision made before either agent starts, or the canvas transferred only when a surface or context asks for it.","files":null}]}